      "summaries": {
        "en": "OpenWrt is a Linux-based operating system for embedded devices, primarily routers, aiming to provide a fully customizable and secure networking platform. Its core strength lies in the use of a writable filesystem and package management, allowing users to install only needed components. Technically, it leverages the Linux kernel's networking stack and a build system that cross-compiles for many architectures. Practically, you can flash it on compatible routers to gain advanced features like VPNs, ad blocking, or traffic shaping, or use it as a base for IoT gateways and mesh networks.",
        "zh": "OpenWrt是基于Linux的嵌入式设备操作系统，专为路由器等网络设备设计，提供高度可定制且安全的网络平台。其核心优势在于可写文件系统与包管理机制，用户可按需安装组件，避免资源浪费。技术层面，它深度利用Linux内核网络栈，并通过交叉编译支持多种硬件架构。实际应用中，可在兼容路由器上刷入OpenWrt，实现VPN、广告拦截、流量整形等高级功能，或作为物联网网关与Mesh网络基础系统。其模块化设计便于开发者扩展自定义功能，是学习嵌入式Linux与网络协议栈的理",
        "es": "OpenWrt is a Linux-based operating system for embedded devices, primarily routers, aiming to provide a fully customizable and secure networking platform. Its core strength lies in the use of a writable filesystem and package management, allowing users to install only needed components. Technically, it leverages the Linux kernel's networking stack and a build system that cross-compiles for many architectures. Practically, you can flash it on compatible routers to gain advanced features like VPNs, ad blocking, or traffic shaping, or use it as a base for IoT gateways and mesh networks.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "openwrt gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "OpenWrt is a Linux-based operating system for embedded devices, primarily routers, aiming to provide a fully customizable and secure networking platform. Its core strength lies in the use of a writable filesystem and package management, allowing users to install only needed components. Technically, it leverages the Linux kernel's networking stack and a build system that cross-compiles for many architectures. Practically, you can flash it on compatible routers to gain advanced features like VPNs, ad blocking, or traffic shaping, or use it as a base for IoT gateways and mesh networks.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
